    Troubleshooting
  </heading>
  <text>
    <location value="17"/>
    <location value="54"/>
    <location value="216"/>
    <location value="94"/>
    If	you	think	there	is	a	problem	with	the	camera,	first	check	the	following.	 If the items below do not solve your problem, contact a Canon Customer  Support Help Desk.
  </text>
  <heading level="2">
    <location value="17"/>
    <location value="101"/>
    <location value="43"/>
    <location value="112"/>
    Power
  </heading>
  <heading level="3">
    <location value="17"/>
    <location value="119"/>
    <location value="171"/>
    <location value="130"/>
    Nothing	happens	when	the	power	button	is	pressed.
  </heading>
  <list ordered="false">
    <list_text>
      <location value="16"/>
      <location value="135"/>
      <location value="136"/>
      <location value="146"/>
      •	 Confirm	that	the	battery	pack	is	charged	( =    10).
    </list_text>
    <list_text>
      <location value="16"/>
      <location value="150"/>
      <location value="189"/>
      <location value="160"/>
      •	 Confirm	that	the	battery	pack	is	inserted	facing	the	correct	way	( =    11).
    </list_text>
    <list_text>
      <location value="17"/>
      <location value="164"/>
      <location value="178"/>
      <location value="175"/>
      •	 Confirm	that	the	memory	card/battery	cover	is	fully	closed	( =    11).
    </list_text>
    <list_text>
      <location value="16"/>
      <location value="180"/>
      <location value="222"/>
      <location value="202"/>
      •	 Dirty battery terminals reduce battery performance. Try cleaning the terminals with a  cotton swab and reinserting the battery pack a few times.
    </list_text>
  </list>
